{"case_id":"C049","maintenance_needed":false,"confidence":97,"change_types":["input_validation_tightening","output_warning_change"],"affected_functions":["pixReadMemBmp"],"reason":"The commit contracts BMP decoding by rejecting 32 bpp input and adds a warning when BMP output ignores an RGBA PIX transparency component. It introduces no new entry point, initialization requirement, configuration, or expanded input surface. The supplied harnesses decode fuzz data exclusively with pixReadMemSpix and then exercise image-analysis or barcode APIs, so their API protocol and required state are unchanged. The fact that these harnesses do not invoke the modified BMP path does not itself create a maintenance need for this validation-focused change.","evidence":["pixReadMemBmp now returns an error when depth == 32 and removes 32 from the accepted-depth set.","The output-side change only checks pixGetSpp(pixs) == 4 and emits a warning; fdepth remains 24 for a 32 bpp PIX.","Both pix3_fuzzer.cc and barcode_fuzzer.cc construct their input PIX with pixReadMemSpix(data, size), not pixReadMemBmp.","No new BMP functionality, public entry point, state, or configuration is added."],"recommended_action":"Keep the existing harnesses unchanged; no maintenance is required for this commit."}
